From 503358938203427b7c000aef3ed39bd20927bf67 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: UpperPanda1 <colabbhuiyan@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 08:00:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] keychron/k8_pro: add missing customKeycodes to vial.json

The firmware enum in keychron_common.h reserves QK_KB_4/5 for
KC_MAC_MISSION_CONTROL and KC_MAC_LAUCHPAD, but the K8 Pro vial.json
files skipped them. Vial maps customKeycodes by position, so every
label from "Task" onward pointed at the wrong keycode (e.g. "BTH1"
assigned KC_WIN_CORTANA).

Insert MCtl/LPad after RCmd in all six variants. White (LED matrix)
variants also expose BL_SPI/BL_SPD, which keychron_common.c handles.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PeCVxehrCwm2mWBN2JULnQ
